tmux with everything removed except tabs. for running coding agents and ssh work.

no prefix key, no panes, no copy mode. chrome shortcuts only:

    ⌘T        new tab (pick claude / codex / pi / opencode / shell)
    ⌘W        close tab
    ⌘1-9      jump to tab
    ⌃⇥ ⌃⇧⇥    next / previous tab

usage:

    $ git clone https://github.com/sueszli/tmux-tabs ~/.tmux-tabs
    $ cat ~/.tmux-tabs/ghostty >> ~/.config/ghostty/config
    $ alias tabs=~/.tmux-tabs/tmux-tabs
    $ tabs

closing the terminal leaves the agents running. `tabs` reattaches.

runs on its own socket, your ~/.tmux.conf is untouched.

needs a terminal that can send ⌘ as escape sequences (ghostty config included;
kitty/wezterm/iterm2 work the same way). terminal.app can't, use ⌥ there instead.
